age).","Above the world average: 17% of the works per year have an FWCI above 1.","Not cited: on average 44% of these works have FWCI 0, meaning no citations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 1 of 1 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2020: mean 0.57, median 0.24, top work 2.81. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2024–2026 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet.","Small base: the values for 2020 and 2024–2026 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2020–2022 have a median of 0 citations each.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2020 have at least 5 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2020–2026 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 2 of 2 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2020: mean 1.8, median 0, top work 9. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2026 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2020, 2022 and 2024–2026 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care."]}}}